"""
Siril Wizard – Automatic Multi-Session Processing
© 2026 Cyril Richard – GPL-3.0-or-later

This script automates the entire preprocessing phase. It is designed to be
extremely easy to use. Users simply need to drag and drop their data, whether
it has been sorted beforehand or not. The script requires FITS files containing
a structured header with the appropriate keywords. It does not work with images
that do not include these keywords.
It works very well with files generated by software such as "NINA," "CCDCiel,"
"Asiair," and probably many others.


Pipeline:
  Phase 1 – Master Bias    : per session (skip if pre-existing master found)
  Phase 2 – Master Darks   : per session (skip if pre-existing / external folder)
  Phase 3 – Master Flats   : per session × filter (bias-calibrated before stacking)
  Phase 4 – Calibrate Lights: per session × filter
  Phase 5 – Register & Stack: per filter, merge all sessions, register, stack, save

  version 1.0.11

  1.0.0  First release
  1.0.1  Don't use temporary file system; do all operations in the cwd
  1.0.2  Flats are now stacked with multiplicative normalization
         Darks are grouped by exposure time (one master per exptime per session)
         Fix calibration tree: flats and darks now separated by session in the
         tree view, matching the per-session grouping used by the pipeline engine
  1.0.3  Skip flats for filters not used by any light frame
         Skip darks for exposure times not required by lights or flats
  1.0.4  Tree view now groups darks by exposure time within each session
         Pre-existing master darks are now stored per-exposure, so multiple
         pre-stacked master darks per session (different exptimes) all work
         _dark_arg now picks the closest in-session master dark when no exact
         exposure match exists, with a warning when the mismatch exceeds 5%
  1.0.5  _dark_arg now matches darks across sessions: any master with the
         right exposure is reused, regardless of which session it came from.
         Darks depend on camera state, not date, so this resolves the case
         where lights from one night had no usable dark just because the
         darks were captured on a different night.
  1.0.6  Fix light calibration
  1.0.7  Fix the test for FILTER when Empty or None is used as a keyword value
         Fix bug when no (master-) darks are provided in OSC preprocessing
  1.0.8  Support capture devices that omit IMAGETYP (DWARF 3)
  1.0.9  Save aligned files according to the STACK_SAVE_PATTERN
  1.0.10 Add the option to save master files
  1.0.11 Sanitise a string for use in directory and sequence names
"""

